---
/**
 * The visual-regression fixture page, rendered through the real blog pipeline.
 *
 * Why it exists: the committed Playwright baselines used to be full-page shots of real posts and
 * marketing pages, so every copy edit invalidated ~1 MB of PNGs and every new post added pressure
 * for another baseline. This page exercises the same rehype plugins (download dropdown, theme
 * images, figure rows, comparison slider, inline icons) plus Shiki and smartypants, on ~10 KB of
 * deliberately frozen content, so a baseline moves only when the machinery moves.
 *
 * Why it's a page import rather than a blog collection entry: staying out of `src/content/blog`
 * keeps it off /blog, out of rss.xml, and away from the /og/[slug].png route, so no production
 * listing has to learn to filter it. It's `noindex` and excluded from the sitemap (astro.config.ts),
 * so it ships as an unlinked, uncrawled page.
 *
 * Keep in sync: `e2e/visual.spec.ts` shoots this page, and `src/fixtures/visual-fixture.md` is the
 * content. Adding a markdown transform means adding a block there, not shooting another real post.
 *
 * oxfmt reformats the fixture markdown like any other file (it joins the figure-row and slider image
 * lines onto one line, which `rehypeBlogMedia` still parses). No guard needed: if a formatter change
 * ever did break a transform, the committed baselines are exactly what would catch it.
 */
import BlogLayout from '../layouts/BlogLayout.astro'
import { Content, frontmatter } from '../fixtures/visual-fixture.md'
---

<BlogLayout
    title={frontmatter.title}
    description={frontmatter.description}
    date={frontmatter.date}
    noindex
>
    <Content />
</BlogLayout>
